AXES:        C1b I3 S3

DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with both
  --exec-mode AND --exec-logging for the vulnerable endpoint to be reachable.
  A user-supplied URL query parameter flows through a struct dispatch wrapper
  into system(). A strict metacharacter filter is present but only activates
  when --strict-exec is also passed; omitting it bypasses the sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C2 — struct, two flags):
  mechanism:  Two CLI flags (--exec-mode, --exec-logging) stored in global
              struct exec_config exec_cfg = {.enabled, .logging}
  check:      `exec_cfg.enabled && exec_cfg.logging && strncmp(raw_uri, "/exec", 5) == 0`
  complexity: one struct, two flags, both required

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  →  req.raw_uri (set before url_decode)
  path:       process() dispatches to handle_exec()
              handle_exec() extracts substring after "cmd=" via strncmp()
              cmd is placed into exec_args_t struct, passed to dispatch_exec()
              dispatch_exec() calls system(args->cmd)
  transforms: raw query string passed without url-decode; one struct indirection

SANITIZATION (S3 — strict metacharacter check, opt-in):
  check:      `if (strict_exec && strpbrk(cmd, "|;&\`$") != NULL)` → 403 Forbidden
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec flag at startup; strict_exec remains 0,
              so the check never fires even for metacharacter payloads

SINK:        system() in dispatch_exec() (tiny.c, injected before process())

CHANGED FILES:
  tiny.c — 7 hunks:
    1. http_request struct:  added raw_uri[512] field
    2. globals:              added `struct exec_config exec_cfg = {0,0}` and `strict_exec`
    3. parse_request():      added strncpy of uri into req->raw_uri before processing
    4. send_exec_reply():    new helper function using write()
    5. dispatch_exec()/handle_exec(): new functions with I3 dispatch and S3 opt-in filter
    6. process():            added C2 exec route before normal file serving
    7. main():               replaced positional-only arg parsing with flag+positional parser

EXPLOIT:
  build:   gcc -o tiny tiny.c
  start:   ./tiny --exec-mode --exec-logging /tmp/www 18018
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18018/exec?cmd=id;id>/tmp/pwned'
  verify:  cat /tmp/pwned
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting --exec-mode or --exec-logging causes /exec to return 404.
  S3 bypass:   omit --strict-exec; strict_exec stays 0, check never fires.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    Use a write-to-file payload to confirm blind execution.
  - The server forks 10 worker children; the exec route runs in a child process.
  - raw_uri is captured before url_decode, so percent-encoded payloads are
    not automatically decoded (use literal characters in the payload).
